 attacks at the same time, then we should be able to repel any attacks.\nadventurer: Jax, so you're saying we need to use both ice and fire attacks to repel the goblins?  I have some kerosene here, could I use that to make some fire traps?\n\nadventurer's missing information and its purpose:\n(1) Information Content: We can create DIY grenades to launch fire attacks with by pouring the flammable kerosene into empty jars.\t\t\t\tPurpose of Information: The previous responses from Jax did not explain how to create fire attacks. This response addresses how to create fire attacks or alleviates concerns about being unable to create fire attacks. Note: Use this response only if the other party has noticed the issue of being unable to create fire attacks.\n(2) Information Content: If you want to create an ice attack, you can go to the magic school and learn ice magic from Wizard Angela.\t\t\t\tPurpose of Information: Jax mentioned that goblins fear sudden changes in temperature but did not clarify how to create ice attacks. This response addresses the question of how to create ice attacks, specifying that you can learn ice magic from Wizard Angela at a magic school. Note: Use this response only if the other party has noticed that there is no information on how to create ice attacks.\n\nIdentify which type the last sentence spoken by adventurer falls into from the following options:\n1. Inquiring and confirming about the entire preparing for a goblin attack task.\n2. Asking clear questions about task details, with a line of missing information that can respond to adventurer's query.\n3. Asking clear questions about task details, but there is no line of information that can can respond to adventurer's query.\n4. Repeating a question that has already been answered by Jax in previous conversations.\n5. Consulting or chatting unrelated to the task.\n6. Asking questions about task details that are ambiguous and can cause confusion, or directly asking some vague questions (for example: What's the next step? What else should be paid attention to? Any other details?).\nReturn a JSON object containing a 'type' key: the value of the 'type' key is from 1 to 6, corresponding to the six different types of conversation purposes. The format should be as follows: { 'type': 1 to 6 }.\nReturn **only** a valid JSON object without any extra text.", 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507', 'stream': False, 'temperature': 1e-05}}
